jobs.description:
As a logistics employee, you help keep the logistics process running smoothly. You handle goods with care and make sure everything is ready for shipment. Your main tasks include:

- Handling goods: Loading, unloading, moving, and preparing products for delivery.
- Keeping order: Scanning materials, checking inventory, and organizing the workplace.
- Following rules: Working safely, following instructions, and using protective gear when needed.

- Approximately 3+ years of work-experience in a logistic environment;
- Able to communicate in English B1/B2 level;
- Driving license (car) is preferred;
- Available for working 2 shifts;
- Soft-skills that match with the company-culture: teamplayer, proactive and motivated

Are you looking for a job at a manufacturing company with varied responsibilities? This is a position as an operator working in a 5-shift rotation in the packaging department. In this role, you’ll work as a production worker in a 5-shift rotation at a company in Ittervoort. Your daily tasks will include:

- Operating the (packaging) machine and troubleshooting malfunctions during the packaging process;
- Operating the mixer, where raw materials are blended;
- Working in accordance with HACCP guidelines to ensure food safety;
- Restocking products using a forklift.

You will work in a 5-shift rotation, with the following schedules: 1:45 p.m. – 10:15 p.m., 9:45 p.m. – 6:15 a.m., 5:45 a.m. – 2:15 p.m. (8,5 hours per day).

You can work in various roles, including loader, mixer, filler, and packer. You’ll learn all of this on the job. 

- MBO-level work and thinking skills, preferably in the field of food or engineering. Do you happen to have experience in the food industry? Then you have an edge!;
- Experience operating machinery;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English for safety regulations;
- You have an eye for detail, and you’re also flexible and able to handle stress.

Do you have a forklift certification? That’s a definite plus!

The Re-Use department is different from a typical warehouse operation. Instead of handling standard products, you work with high-value technical components used by ASML.

Your job is to make sure these parts are received, checked, processed and prepared for their next step. Because of the variety of tasks, every day brings something different.

Your responsibilities may include:

- Receiving and checking incoming materials;
- Scanning and processing products in the system;
- Inspecting parts for quality and completeness;
- Sorting and storing materials;
- Picking orders;
- Packing and preparing shipments;
- Processing logistics data accurately.

Whether you already have warehouse experience or are looking for a new opportunity, there are several areas within the department where you can develop your skills.

- Good communication skills in English;
- Full-time availability;
- A positive and motivated attitude;
- Accuracy and attention to detail;
- Warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

SamenvattingDo you see a challenge in loading, unloading and carefully checking freight? Do you want to work in a dynamic, international environment? Become a Warehouse Mail Employee at Schiphol-Rijk, full-time! Good work!Over de functieAs a Warehouse Post employee, you will play an important role in loading and unloading goods and work closely with your team in a dynamic environment. Flexibility, cooperation and customer orientation are key. What will you do?
- Mail acceptance and processing;
- Sorting mail bags and parcels;
- Performing light administrative tasks;
- ULD assembly and disassembly;
- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Transport on the platform

You will work in a diverse team and follow a schedule with three different shifts:
- Morning shift: 07:00 - 15:30 
- Afternoon shift: 15:00 - 23:30 
- Night shift: 23:00 - 07:00 

Over het bedrijfAt this leading company, you will have the opportunity to work in a dynamic environment where teamwork and efficiency are key. As a leading player in the logistics sector, the organization offers a challenging work environment where you can further develop your skills and play an important role in the efficient handling of shipments.
Wat wij vragen- Have logistics experience;
- Willing to follow internal courses;
- Good Command of the Dutch or/and English language;
- Ready to work physically;
- You can obtain a Certificate of No Objection (VGB) ( which we will apply for) meaning you should have at least 8 years of registration within the EU.

These points are very important to start working as a Warehouse Post Employee at Schiphol-Rijk. We are also curious about who you are. Curious about your talents, background and ideas. Surprise us.
Wat wij bieden- € 16.70  € 16,99 gross salary per hour, depending on relevant work experience (including 2,5% year-end bonus) 
- Supplements for evening, night weekend shifts and public holidays, ranging from 125% to 140%
- Holiday allowances of 200%
- Weekly payments with 8.33% vac
